data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"For coordinate j, let ρⱼ be Xⱼᵀ applied to the residual with wⱼ added back, divided by n, and let zⱼ be\n‖Xⱼ‖² divided by n. The new wⱼ is the soft-threshold of ρⱼ at α, divided by zⱼ. Skip any column with\nzⱼ = 0. Repeat full sweeps until the largest coefficient change in one sweep is below `tol`."},"hints_note":null}

